{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-27T09:09:13.313Z","data":{"text":"Task 2 complete. Summary:\n\n**Implemented** `src/core/status/dispatch-keys.ts`:\n- `CardKey` (`key`, `label`, `args`, `asks`), `CardKeys` (`keys` + `manual`).\n- `cardKeys(item)` maps `osq approve/retry/reject/check/verified/show` commands to keys in order (`a`, `r`, `x` asking `reason`, `c`, `p`/`f`, `s`), splitting args on spaces only; unknown-verb and non-`osq` commands go to `manual` unchanged.\n- `formatCardScreen(total, item, card, keys)` renders the `Needs you (n):` header, the card body, the `Keys:` block (`  n  skip`, `  q  quit`), and `Run yourself:` when manual commands exist.\n\n**Refactored** `src/core/status/dispatch-text.ts` to export `formatDispatchCardBody(item, card)` and rebuilt `cardLines` on it, keeping `osq inbox` output byte-identical.\n\n**Added** `tests/dispatch-keys.test.ts` covering all five \"Card keys\" scenarios via `readDispatchItems` on temporary projects, including the real git worktree land case.\n\nBoth verifies pass:\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/dispatch-keys.test.ts` → 5/5 pass\n- `pnpm verify` → typechecks, build, full suite, and lint pass\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/099-inbox-cards/.run/results/2.md`."}}
